AB  - A 38-year-old woman presented with 2 months of dry cough, progressive shortness 
      of breath, central chest pain, nausea, vomiting, and dizziness. She was 
      previously healthy and was not taking any medications. She denied fever, night 
      sweats, or weight loss. She had a two pack-year smoking history and had quit 
      smoking at 27 years of age. She denied drug use and had no recent travel history. 
      Family history was pertinent for ovarian cancer, breast cancer, and colon cancer.
