TI  - Α 57-Year-Old Woman With ARDS, Cachexia, and a 2-Month Fever.
PG  - e27-e31
LID - S0012-3692(19)30610-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2019.02.328 [doi]
AB  - A 57-year-old homemaker and rural inhabitant of Central Greece (ex-smoker, 25 
      pack-years), was admitted to the ICU because of acute hypoxemic respiratory 
      failure with diffuse bilateral alveolar infiltrates. Her medical history was 
      unremarkable. She had been looking after her mother in a farmhouse with goats and 
      a dog for the previous 6 months. She had not ingested any unpasteurized dairy 
      products. She complained of fever and weight loss (8 kg) over the previous 
      2 months. She developed a nonproductive cough during the past 5 days and was 
      referred to the hospital.
