AB  - A 60-year-old Chinese man was admitted to our hospital with chronic cough for > 
      2 months. His cough was paroxysmal and nonirritating, occasionally productive 
      with some small amounts of white phlegm. He had had a low-grade fever for half a 
      month. There were no night sweats, joint swelling on limbs, pain, rash, or any 
      other discomfort. The patient denied weight loss and decreased appetite.
