TI  - A 33-Year-Old Woman With Altered Mental Status and Elevated Ammonia Level.
PG  - e169-e171
LID - S0012-3692(18)30981-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2018.06.029 [doi]
AB  - A 33-year-old woman was brought to the ED with altered mental status. She was 
      combative on presentation but spontaneously progressed into a comatose state and 
      was intubated for airway protection. Naloxone failed to improve her mental 
      status. When family was reached, they reported a history of seizures that were 
      controlled on treatment.
