TI  - A 35-Year-Old Woman With Acute Pleuritic Chest Pain and an Unusual Mediastinal 
      Opacity.
PG  - e17-e20
LID - S0012-3692(18)31195-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2018.07.036 [doi]
AB  - A 35-year-old woman came to the ED following 2 days of chest pain. She was a 
      nonsmoker, taking no medications, and not using a contraceptive pill. The patient 
      had no history of recent travel but had given birth (full-term pregnancy) 
      4 months earlier. She described nonradiating, left-sided pleuritic chest pain 
      with no associated dyspnea, cough, sputum, or sweating.
