TI  - A 3-Year-Old Girl With a Mediastinal Mass.
PG  - e13-e16
LID - S0012-3692(18)32248-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2018.07.042 [doi]
AB  - A 3-year-old girl was referred to a pediatric pulmonologist for dyspnea and 
      recurrent upper respiratory tract infections (RTIs). The patient was born full 
      term to unrelated Dutch parents after an uneventful pregnancy and birth. The year 
      before presentation, she had suffered from pneumonia and > 10 upper RTIs. Apart 
      from the recurrent RTIs, which started in infancy, her medical history was not 
      significant and did not include allergies or eczema. An adenotonsillectomy was 
      performed at the age of 2 years, and she was treated with multiple antibiotic 
      regimens and inhalation therapy with salbutamol and corticosteroids, with no 
      relief of symptoms.
