LID - S0012-3692(18)30398-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2018.02.030 [doi]
AB  - A 68-year-old man with a history of chronic lymphocytic leukemia well controlled 
      on ibrutinib, hypertension, obesity, and a remote history of smoking (10 
      pack-years) presented with increasing dyspnea on exertion and cough. He had 
      previously finished two courses of oral antibiotics for his symptoms without 
      significant improvement. On presentation, he had no fevers or sputum production.
