TI  - Familial Chronic Thromboembolic Pulmonary Hypertension.
PG  - e99-e101
LID - S0012-3692(15)00043-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2015.09.017 [doi]
AB  - Chronic thromboembolic pulmonary hypertension (CTEPH) is an uncommon disease that 
      is the most serious complication associated with unresolved pulmonary embolism. 
      This disease has several risk factors, but no familial pattern has been 
      described. Few thrombophilic conditions have been reported to increase risk of 
      CTEPH, and none of the hereditary thrombophilias causes this disease. The reason 
      CTEPH develops in some patients after pulmonary embolism remains unknown. We 
      describe a 54-year-old woman and her maternal aunt who both underwent pulmonary 
      thromboendarterectomy for CTEPH. This represents the first description of 
      familial CTEPH.
