TI  - A 45-Year-Old Woman With 3 Weeks of Cough and Night Sweats.
PG  - e87-90
LID - S0012-3692(15)00029-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2015.08.014 [doi]
AB  - A 45-year-old woman who received a renal transplant 7 years prior presented with 
      a 3-week history of low-grade fever, night sweats, and a dry cough with scant 
      sputum production. Additionally, she reported generalized weakness and increased 
      fatigability. She denied hemoptysis or weight loss, and there had been no change 
      in medication or foreign travel. She had no history of latent tuberculosis or 
      sick contacts. She had recently relocated to Baton Rouge, Louisiana. She was 
      sexually active with her boyfriend who worked as a prison guard. She also 
      reported that she was briefly incarcerated 7 years ago shortly after her renal 
      transplantation. Her immunosuppression consisted of tacrolimus, mycophenolate, 
      and prednisone.
