TI  - Pediatric Insomnia.
PG  - 1332-9
LID - S0012-3692(15)00015-X [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.15-0605 [doi]
AB  - Insomnia in children is complex and frequently multifactorial. This review 
      discusses the major categories of insomnia as well as common causes. The 
      consequences of insomnia, including issues with mood, behavior, and cognition, 
      are discussed. Sleep disorders are much more prevalent in certain pediatric 
      populations, such as children with autism spectrum disorders. The evaluation of 
      insomnia in children includes a focused history and examination and occasionally 
      actigraphy or polysomnography. Behavioral and pharmacological therapies are 
      discussed, as are future directions for research and clinical practice.
