LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2018.07.010 [doi]
AB  - The performance of a lumbar puncture is generally associated with a high rate of 
      success and a favorable risk profile. Nonetheless, the use of ultrasound for 
      procedural guidance has been demonstrated to reduce the rate of failure and the 
      risk of specific complications, especially in patients with difficult surface 
      anatomy. Many individual ultrasound techniques have been described in the 
      literature; this article presents a systematic approach for incorporating these 
      tools into bedside practice and includes a series of illustrative figures and 
      narrated video presentations to demonstrate the techniques described.
