TI  - A 74-Year-Old Man Presenting With Cough, Malaise, and Mediastinal 
      Lymphadenopathy.
PG  - e37-e40
LID - S0012-3692(17)31477-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2017.08.023 [doi]
AB  - A 74-year-old white male farmer was admitted from his primary care physician's 
      office after he presented with symptoms of cough productive of clear sputum, 
      malaise, weakness, fatigue, and shortness of breath on exertion for 3 weeks. He 
      was an ex-smoker with a history of hypertension, hyperlipidemia, and coronary 
      artery bypass graft surgery. He did not report any chills, night sweats, or 
      fevers during this presentation.
