AB  - A 57-year-old man was referred to the ED for wake-up right-sided hemiparesis, 
      hypoesthesia, dysarthria, and a National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale score 
      of 7. Urgent CT brain scanning showed an ischemic lesion of the left temporal and 
      insular lobes. The patient was admitted to the stroke unit, and acetylsalicylic 
      acid 300 mg and low-molecular-weight heparin 6,000 IU were administered.
