TI  - A 33-Year-Old Woman With a Fluorodeoxyglucose-Avid Left Lower Lobe Mass.
PG  - e119-e122
LID - S0012-3692(16)62337-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2016.10.049 [doi]
AB  - A 33-year-old woman of Latin American origin was referred to our department by 
      her primary care physician for a left lower lobe mass, which was incidentally 
      found on a CT scan of her abdomen. The patient had complaints of abdominal pain 
      for which she underwent imaging of her abdomen. Review of systems was negative 
      for any respiratory complaints, and she denied any history of cigarette smoking 
      or recreational drug use.
