TI  - A 28-Year-Old Woman With Branching Opacity and Chest Pain.
PG  - e85-e89
LID - S0012-3692(17)30004-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2016.12.022 [doi]
AB  - A 28-year-old female patient presented through her primary care physician with 
      symptoms of atypical chest pain and chronic cough. Her pain was described as 
      pleuritic and intermittently radiating to the right arm. Her medical history was 
      significant for recurrent respiratory infections, gastritis, and a left ovarian 
      cyst treated with ipsilateral salpingo-oophorectomy. She denied any history of 
      smoking, known lung disease, or extrapulmonary infections.
