TI  - Sleep Tracking, Wearable Technology, and Opportunities for Research and Clinical 
      Care.
PG  - 732-43
LID - S0012-3692(16)48652-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2016.04.016 [doi]
AB  - Consumer-driven sleep-tracking technologies are becoming increasingly popular 
      with patients with sleep disorders and the general population. As the list of 
      sleep-tracking technologies continues to grow, clinicians and researchers are 
      faced with new challenges and opportunities to incorporate these technologies 
      into current practice. We review diagnostic tools used in sleep medicine clinical 
      practice, discuss categories of consumer sleep-tracking technologies currently 
      available, and explore the advantages and disadvantages of each. Potential uses 
      of consumer sleep-tracking technologies to enhance sleep medicine patient care 
      and research are also discussed.
