TI  - Persistent Challenges in Pediatric Pulmonary Hypertension.
PG  - 226-36
LID - S0012-3692(16)00469-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2016.01.007 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary hypertension and related pulmonary vascular diseases cause significant 
      morbidities and high mortality and present many unique challenges toward 
      improving outcomes in neonates, infants, and children. Differences between 
      pediatric and adult disease are reflected in controversies regarding etiologies, 
      classification, epidemiology, diagnostic evaluations, and therapeutic 
      interventions. This brief review highlights several key topics reflecting recent 
      advances in the field and identifies persistent gaps in our understanding of 
      clinical pediatric pulmonary hypertension.
