TI  - CPAP in the Perioperative Setting: Evidence of Support.
PG  - 586-597
LID - S0012-3692(15)00057-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.15-1777 [doi]
AB  - OSA is a commonly encountered comorbid condition in surgical patients. The risk 
      of cardiopulmonary complications is increased by two to threefold with OSA. Among 
      the different treatment options for OSA, CPAP is an efficacious modality. This 
      review examines the evidence regarding the use of CPAP in the preoperative and 
      postoperative periods in surgical patients with diagnosed and undiagnosed OSA.
