TI  - A 38-Year-Old Man With Obesity, Intermittent Tachycardia, and One Episode of 
      Syncope.
PG  - e22-e25
LID - S0012-3692(15)50055-X [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.14-1812 [doi]
AB  - A 38-year-old man with history of diabetes, hypertension, hyperlipidemia, and 
      obesity was referred to the electrophysiology clinic for evaluation of infrequent 
      palpitations and remote history of syncope. The patient described a sensation of 
      racing of the heart, which lasted about 30 min to 1 h and occurred several times 
      over the past year. This was associated with a sense of anxiety and shortness of 
      breath and appeared to resolve spontaneously. The patient also experienced one 
      episode of syncope in the past while enjoying a barbecue on a hot summer day. He 
      did not recall if this episode was accompanied by palpitations, however, the 
      previously mentioned symptoms prompted the consultation. Upon further questioning 
      the patient also reported experiencing fatigue. He stated that he noted decreased 
      energy and frequent daytime sleepiness.
