TI  - The association of direct thrombin inhibitor anticoagulants with cardiac 
      thromboses.
PG  - 21-24
LID - S0012-3692(15)30231-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.14-2028 [doi]
AB  - Direct thrombin inhibitor (anti-factor IIa) anticoagulants, now established for 
      treatment and prevention of cardiac thromboembolism and VTE, have been repeatedly 
      associated with a significantly increased frequency of thrombosis on abnormal 
      cardiac endothelium when compared head-to-head with indirectly acting therapeutic 
      anticoagulants in studies of sufficient patient number and duration. Although 
      there is uncertainty as to the mechanism, the weight of evidence as a class 
      effect warrants prescribing effective anticoagulants other than direct thrombin 
      inhibitors.
