TI  - Between a Rock and an Airspace: Pneumothorax After Extracorporeal Shock Wave 
      Lithotripsy for Renal Stones in a Patient With Cystic Fibrosis.
PG  - e61-e63
LID - S0012-3692(18)30470-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2018.03.023 [doi]
AB  - Renal disease is a well-recognized manifestation of cystic fibrosis (CF) and 
      people with CF are at increased risk of nephrolithiasis. Lithotripsy is the 
      preferred treatment but has occasionally been associated with pulmonary 
      complications. Here we report the case of a person with CF who developed a 
      pneumothorax soon after lithotripsy and discuss the potential mechanism of 
      injury. We hope this case highlights some of the additional considerations 
      clinicians should take into account when managing patients with advanced 
      pulmonary disease in CF.
