AB  - A 70-year-old woman presents with recurrent idiopathic chylothorax refractory to 
      both medical and surgical treatment. To our knowledge, this is the first reported 
      case where midodrine, an alpha-1 receptor agonist, was used as an adjunctive 
      therapy for idiopathic chylothorax resulting in both a radiographic and clinical 
      response.
