AB  - A 77-year-old woman presented to the hospital with symptoms of progressive 
      shortness of breath with associated right-sided pleuritic pain. The patient had 
      begun noting dyspnea on exertion, limiting her ability to go on hikes over the 
      few days prior to admission. Her medical history is significant for carcinoid 
      tumor status postresection in 2012 without recurrence. She has no history of 
      thromboembolism or clotting disorders, and she has no history of smoking or drug 
      abuse. Current medications include amlodipine, celecoxib, hydrochlorothiazide, 
      and rosuvastatin.
