TI  - Bronchiectasis Complicating Lung Volume Reduction Coil Treatment.
PG  - e57-e60
LID - S0012-3692(17)31063-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2017.04.189 [doi]
AB  - Endoscopic lung volume reduction has emerged over the past several years as a 
      promising technique to improve the respiratory functional status of patients with 
      advanced emphysema. Nevertheless, the procedure may be associated with various 
      complications; among them, the development of bronchiectasis related to the coils 
      has not yet been described. We report the case of a patient with emphysema who 
      developed localized bronchiectasis at the site of coil insertion several months 
      after lung volume reduction coil treatment.
