TI  - Tracheobronchopathy From Inhaled Corticosteroids.
PG  - 1296-1305
LID - S0012-3692(17)31429-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2017.08.013 [doi]
AB  - Inhaled corticosteroids (ICSs) have become the mainstay of asthma control. They 
      are also recommended as an add-on therapy to long-acting beta agonists and 
      anticholinergics in moderate to severe COPD with recurrent exacerbations. 
      Ultimately this clinical practice has led to the widespread use of ICSs, which 
      are supported by a more favorable side effect profile than that of systemic 
      steroids.
