TI  - A 19-Year-Old College Student With Headache, Photophobia, and Flulike Illness.
PG  - e95-e98
LID - S0012-3692(16)62335-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2016.10.047 [doi]
AB  - A 19-year-old previously healthy man presented, minimally responsive, in 
      respiratory distress to an ED after a 2-week history of headache, photophobia, 
      and neck stiffness. Associated symptoms included low-grade fevers, malaise, and 
      dark urine. He had no recent travel, ill contacts, consumption of undercooked 
      meat, new sexual contacts, or illicit drug use. The patient resided in a campus 
      dormitory and did not consume alcohol or tobacco.
