PG  - e175-e180
LID - S0012-3692(15)50125-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.14-2680 [doi]
AB  - Seven years after left hemicolectomy and radical lymph nodal dissection followed 
      by adjuvant chemotherapy for colorectal cancer (histotype, adenocarcinoma; stage, 
      pT3N2M0; grading, G2), a slight increase in carcinoembryonic antigen levels (6.2 
      ng/mL; range, 0-5 ng/mL) was detected in a 79-year-old man. He was a heavy smoker 
      with history of an interstitial fibrotic lung disease with associated areas of 
      emphysema.
