TI  - An unusual case of postpartum dyspnea.
PG  - e38-e43
LID - S0012-3692(15)30200-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.14-0841 [doi]
AB  - A 40-year-old South Asian woman was admitted in active labor at 38 weeks' 
      gestation. She had an unremarkable medical history with routine prenatal care, 
      negative HIV testing results, and an uneventful pregnancy. She received a 
      Bacillus Calmette-Guérin vaccine during childhood and reportedly had a subsequent 
      positive purified protein-derivative test result 1 year prior to conception. She 
      never smoked and had seven normal term pregnancies.
