TI  - An 84-Year-Old Man With Progressive Dyspnea and an Abnormal Chest CT Scan.
PG  - e45-e49
LID - S0012-3692(17)30384-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2017.03.013 [doi]
AB  - An 84-year-old man without a history of smoking presented with progressive 
      dyspnea of 6 months' duration accompanied by fatigue and unintentional weight 
      loss. He denied fever, chills, chest pain, hemoptysis, rash, joint pains, or 
      muscle aches. He had multiple hospitalizations for similar presentations that 
      were diagnosed as pneumonia. History was significant for diastolic heart failure, 
      hypertension, and type 2 diabetes mellitus.
