TI  - Organizing Pneumonia in an Adult With Chronic Recurrent Noninfectious 
      Osteomyelitis: A Case Report and Literature Review.
PG  - e21-e24
LID - S0012-3692(17)30815-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2017.04.172 [doi]
AB  - Chronic recurrent multifocal osteomyelitis (CRMO) is an idiopathic inflammatory 
      disorder primarily of children and adolescents that is characterized by 
      multifocal nonpyogenic relapsing and remitting inflammatory bone lesions. 
      Pulmonary abnormalities are rarely associated with CRMO, with two reported cases 
      of consolidation on chest CT that occurred in children. We present a case of 
      organizing pneumonia in an adult patient with CRMO. The concurrent worsening of 
      pulmonary and bone disease suggests that CRMO may be a rare cause of organizing 
      pneumonia.
