TI  - Persistent Lobar Atelectasis in a Patient With Chronic Hoarseness.
PG  - e107-e113
LID - S0012-3692(17)30159-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2017.01.029 [doi]
AB  - A 61-year-old woman presented for outpatient evaluation of a 1-week history of 
      fever and upper respiratory symptoms. She denied tobacco use, weight loss, 
      hemoptysis, chronic cough, or recent travel and was in otherwise good health. Her 
      medical history was insignificant except for her chronic hoarseness from a prior 
      laryngeal disease. She denied any worsening hoarseness or any other vocal 
      changes. She did report a positive family history of squamous cell lung cancer in 
      her father.
