TI  - A 54-Year-Old Man With Lingual Granuloma and Multiple Pulmonary Excavated 
      Nodules.
PG  - e13-e16
LID - S0012-3692(16)53665-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2016.07.026 [doi]
AB  - A 54-year-old French man was admitted for evaluation of a chronic nodular lesion 
      of the tongue and mandibular lymphadenopathy. He reported active tobacco and 
      cannabis smoking as well as excessive alcohol use. He also reported frequent use 
      of cocaine for several months and a past addiction to IV heroin. He had traveled 
      abroad as a journalist and lived for several months in Columbia and Venezuela 12 
      years ago. His medical history included chronic hepatitis C infection 
      successfully treated with interferon and ribavirin 6 years ago and high BP.
