TI  - A 37-Year-Old Man With Nonresolving Pneumonia and Endobronchial Lesion.
PG  - e52-e55
LID - S0012-3692(15)50363-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.14-1963 [doi]
AB  - A previously healthy, immunocompetent 37-year-old man was hospitalized with a 
      3-month history of intermittent fevers and cough with mucopurulent sputum 
      preceded by flu-like symptoms. Five episodes of similar symptoms had prompted two 
      hospitalizations and three courses of outpatient antibiotics. The fever would 
      subside with treatment but intermittent dry cough persisted. There was no history 
      of weight loss, night sweats, wheezing, arthralgia, skin rash, hemoptysis, recent 
      travel, sick contacts, or high-risk sexual behavior. He was a nonsmoker with no 
      alcohol or recreational drug use. He was an accountant in the military with no 
      history of significant organic or inorganic dust exposures.
