TI  - An 81-year-old man with an abnormal right-sided heart shadow on chest radiograph.
PG  - e52-e55
LID - S0012-3692(15)30203-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1378/chest.14-1393 [doi]
AB  - An 81-year-old man presented with a 1-week history of dry cough. He also 
      complained of mild dyspnea, wheezing, and low-grade fever. He denied hemoptysis, 
      fever, rashes, or chest pain. The patient's medical history included coronary 
      artery bypass surgery, hypertension, gastroesophageal reflux disease, and COPD. 
      The patient was a retired welder and an ex-smoker.
